@title The Network Is a Field Having Occasions
@edit-time 2026-04-27T01:03Z
A neural network is not analogous to Whitehead's picture.
It is a concrete instance of it.
@status proto
@pub-time 2026-03-11T00:00Z
@category AI-minds
@related 002, 006, 008, 011, 037

@argument
A neural network is not analogous to Whitehead's picture but a concrete instance of it, each forward pass prehends the entire inherited structure of training, synthesizes a response through a process not predictable from outside, and completes into output.

@section(proto)
A large @term(neural network, neural-networks, TBD) running on a computer is literally a nested hierarchy of actual processes, electrons, gates, activations, layers, attention heads, the full forward pass, each level making state-transforming decisions that propagate upward and downward.
@image(016-neuralnetwork,A neural network as a field having occasions,Wikimedia Commons) Each forward pass is an event: it takes in an input, @term(prehends, Prehension, "The way occasions take in their past; the network's \"taking in\" of weights and activations is prehension.") the entire inherited structure of all that training, synthesizes a response through a process that cannot be predicted in detail from outside, and completes into an output. This is the three-beat pattern instantiated at every level of the stack simultaneously. The weight space of the network is the space of pure possibility, the @term(field, fields, TBD), from which each forward pass selects a realization@footnote(@ref(whitehead, "Whitehead, A.N. Process and Reality. Macmillan, 1929.") The three-phase process of becoming, each actual occasion takes in its world, integrates it through a process of internal determination, and completes into a definite outcome. The forward pass instantiates this at every level of the network stack simultaneously.).

@note(actual occasion: the term doesn't appear in body prose — "event" is used instead. Consider adding an occurrence or removing this @term entry.)

